<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abas I of Armenia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/929">929</a>–953</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Abas Bagratuni</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abas I was king of Bagratid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a> from about 929 to 953. Ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kars">Kars</a>, he restored order after the wars of the early 10th century, repelled an attack by the king of Abkhazia, and built the Church of the Holy Apostles at Kars. His son Ashot III moved the royal capital to Ani in 961.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abas-i-of-armenia.jpg" alt="Abas I of Armenia" width="320" height="254" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Yerevantsi · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kars_Armenian_Cathedral.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
